  "preflight": [
    "Match the HD-1910-C001 servo, Radxa ZERO 3W 2GB/no-eMMC/header and the October 15 AMP2.0 HAT and IMU projects. This is NOT an ESP32 build.",
    "Read the 3MF five-plate print layout and verify geometry scale; some standalone STLs use tiny coordinate ranges. Use TPU for the sole/tire plate, not the saved PLA preset.",
    "Select either HUB-clamping or snap-fit battery holder, and confirm the designed IMU mounting pattern and bearing sizes.",
    "Treat original purchases as historical engineering examples, not proof of U.S. stock, current price or drop-ship orderability.",
    "Do not apply battery or servo power until polarities, grounds, fuse, 3-pin pinouts and total stall-current budget are verified."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Open the credited original English guide, confirm the exact October 15 AMP2.0 connector variant and print-layout release.",
    "Download the original five-plate 3MF and STL source set. Inspect model scale, PLA versus TPU materials and choose one battery holder before slicing.",
    "Assemble the 15 HD-1910-C001 servos and correct bearings with the printed chassis, securing cables with strain relief.",
    "Inspect or fabricate the original HAT and IMU PCB revisions; flash the correct STM32 IMU firmware before connecting the servo bus.",
    "Mount the Radxa ZERO 3W, IMX219 camera, VL53L5CX V2 sensor, speaker and protected NP-F550 supply.",
    "Validate battery voltage/polarity, bus-pin mapping, connector pitch and independent power-up of each device.",
    "Configure source-matched Linux/robot software, then calibrate servo IDs and joint limits without loading the legs.",
    "Run conservative support/standing tests before source-guided walking and optional roller/reinforcement-learning demos."
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "Check that each servo ID and range matches the rig without linkage binding.",
    "Bring up the IMU and HAT with connector/supply checks before loading the printed robot.",
    "Record safe stand, walk and recovery behavior in a bounded test area.",
    "Verify camera, ToF and battery power with source-matched drivers.",
    "Cross-check printed foot configuration and optional roller bearings against the 3MF source."
  ],
  "agentTasks": [
    "Start with builds/microduck-robot/README.md and follow upstream release URLs; do not use generic ESP32 firmware.",
    "Reconcile exact supplier options against HD-1910-C001, Radxa ZERO 3W no-eMMC, IMX219 160-degree lens, VL53L5CX V2 and AMP2.0 connector variant.",
    "Inspect EasyEDA Pro .epro2 schematic/PCB before manufacturing and run ERC/DRC with the current BOM and board revisions.",
    "Check the RAR/SHA256 manifest and 3MF units, PLA/TPU plate selection and mechanical fit. Do not infer exact print quantity from 36 STL filenames.",
    "Keep Squarespace/Doroppu import/checkout disabled until verified exact supplier variants and U.S. test orders."
  ],
  "caution": "Advanced electromechanical build with lithium-ion batteries, moving servos and custom PCBs. This is an attributed independent project, not a bench-tested MAKHEX kit. Do not replace Radxa with an ESP32, mix EH2.5/AMP2.0 connectors or assume raw STL units equal millimeters."
}
